From 707a7c83e159bd69c3728d0b880d9d202c374574 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:08:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan : add the S-X8 v4.3 kernel for GGML_TYPE_SX8 (57)

WI-1692 landed the S-X8 CPU decoder and Vulkan declined all 14 type_a=sx8
backend-ops cases. On a box whose only compute device is a Radeon 780M that
makes the format unusable, which is the whole point of this commit.

Two shaders and the host wiring, following the TQ3_4S precedent rather than a
type_names row: a type_names entry would demand a mul_mm_funcs.glsl unpack
branch and the whole matmul/coopmat family, and S-X8 reaches prompt processing
through f16 staging (dequant_sx8) exactly as TQ3_4S does.

  dequant_sx8.comp        one thread per 32-weight block; the f16-staging path
  mul_mat_vec_sx8.comp    one thread per weight POSITION, striding whole blocks
                          by BLOCK_SIZE/32. S-X8 has no rotation, so unlike the
                          TQ mat-vecs there is no butterfly, no shared memory
                          and no barrier -- and no 32-thread pin either, which
                          keeps a wave64 device from running half-empty waves.
  types.glsl              block_sx8 (30 B) + sx8_range(), so both shaders share
                          one copy of the range algebra and cannot drift apart.

The 30-byte block is not a multiple of 4. That is already exercised in this
tree -- block_q8_0 is 34 -- and alignment 2 with an even size gives a std430
stride of 30 that matches the C layout.

GET_ROWS, CPY and SET_ROWS are deliberately not generated: nothing quantizes TO
S-X8 on the GPU, so supports_op declines them rather than aborting.

Also wires the quantizer (LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_SX8 = 57, mirroring the ggml type
id): without it nothing can WRITE an S-X8 file, and the format's only published
artifact is a 26.1 GB file this box cannot hold.

arifi_sync_check.py's QUANT_K count goes 35 -> 36. The gate caught QUANT_K_SX8
on the first build and stopped it, which is the F-110 mechanism working.

Correctness on a Radeon 780M, Vulkan, inside a quiet hold: MUL_MAT 12/12 and
MUL_MAT_ID 2/2 EXECUTED and OK -- the same case set the CPU decoder covers, none
skipped into a green banner. test-quantize-fns is byte-identical to the WI-1692
baseline: same 6 failures in the same 3 pre-existing families, sx8 rows pass.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Taken-from: MarlaLabs S-X8 v4.3 decode arithmetic (carried into the fork by WI-1692, repeated here in GLSL)
Lane: lane-224
(cherry picked from commit f43ba4d4db5d8d74c0f744a5af9b95b8262726b8)
